nylon for Debian
----------------

The daemon's configuration lives in /etc/nylon.conf.  Extra command
line options can be set in /etc/default/nylon (DAEMON_OPTS).

Security defaults worth knowing:

  * Only localhost clients are allowed (Allow-IP=127.0.0.1/32).
    Widen Allow-IP only together with a destination policy if the
    proxy must serve other hosts.

  * Allow-Target-IP/Deny-Target-IP restrict where clients may connect
    (e.g. blocking loopback, link-local and RFC1918 destinations);
    see /etc/nylon.conf and nylon(1).

  * When started as root the daemon drops privileges to the user and
    group configured with User=/Group= (default: nobody).  Privilege
    dropping is skipped when Connecting-Interface names a network
    interface, since SO_BINDTODEVICE requires CAP_NET_RAW.

